       }
      },
      "content": [
       {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Venlafaxine, duloxetine, desvenlafaxine, levomilnacipran"
       }
      ]
     },
     {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "attrs": {
       "indLeft": 0,
       "indRight": 0,
       "indFirst": 0,
       "spaceBefore": 0,
       "spaceAfter": 0,
       "line": null,
       "align": "left",
       "shade": null,
       "borders": null,
       "marker": {
        "text": "•",
        "font": null,
        "marks": [],
        "tabPt": 12
       }
      },
      "content": [
       {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Effective as second-line agents for MDD and all anxiety disorders"
       }
      ]
     },
     {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "attrs": {
       "indLeft": 0,
       "indRight": 0,
       "indFirst": 0,
       "spaceBefore": 0,
       "spaceAfter": 0,
       "line": null,
       "align": "left",
       "shade": null,
       "borders": null,
       "marker": {
        "text": "•",
        "font": null,
        "marks": [],
        "tabPt": 12
       }
      },
      "content": [
       {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Duloxetine could be considered first-line in patients who have depression and anxiety with comorbid neuropathic pain"
       }
      ]
     },
     {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "attrs": {
       "indLeft": 0,
       "indRight": 0,
       "indFirst": 0,
       "spaceBefore": 0,
       "spaceAfter": 0,
       "line": null,
       "align": "left",
       "shade": null,
       "borders": null,
       "marker": {
        "text": "•",
        "font": null,
        "marks": [],
        "tabPt": 12
       }
      },
      "content": [
       {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Side effect profile is similar to SSRIs with one major exception"
       }
      ]
     },
     {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "attrs": {
       "indLeft": 18,
       "indRight": 0,
       "indFirst": 0,
       "spaceBefore": 0,
       "spaceAfter": 0,
       "line": null,
       "align": "left",
       "shade": null,
       "borders": null,
       "marker": {
        "text": "•",
        "font": null,
        "marks": [],
        "tabPt": 12
       }
      },
      "content": [
       {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Hypertension! At higher doses, SNRIs (mostly venlafaxine) have 10% risk of hypertension."
       }
      ]
     },
     {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "attrs": {
       "indLeft": 18,
       "indRight": 0,
       "indFirst": 0,
       "spaceBefore": 0,
       "spaceAfter": 0,
       "line": null,
       "align": "left",
       "shade": null,
       "borders": null,
       "marker": {
        "text": "•",
        "font": null,
        "marks": [],
        "tabPt": 12
       }
      },
      "content": [
       {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Can get tricky on tests – if hypertension is isolated AND NOT CAUSED IN THE CONTEXT OF EATING CERTAIN FOODS/ALCOHOL AT PARTY, it’s more likely to be a side effect to venlafaxine than MAOi."
       }
      ]
     },
     {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "attrs": {
       "indLeft": 18,
       "indRight": 0,
       "indFirst": 0,
       "spaceBefore": 0,
       "spaceAfter": 0,
       "line": null,
       "align": "left",
       "shade": null,
       "borders": null,
       "marker": {
        "text": "•",
        "font": null,
        "marks": [],
        "tabPt": 12
       }
      },
      "content": [
       {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Venlafaxine withdrawal causes “brain zaps” and flulike symptoms in patients. Tests love this factoid for some reason."
       }
      ]
     }
    ]
   }
